<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22261" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-cānesco</span></b> , canŭi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i>, <i>to become white</i>, <i>to turn gray</i> or <i>hoary</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tortaque remigio spumis incanuit unda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					63, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ornusque incanuit albo Flore piri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 71</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gelu magnoque incanuit imbre Caucasus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 6, 611</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum pigra incanuit aetas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 328</span></i>
			.</div>
